2. Problem statement extracted from the research
Traditional Ant Colony Optimization algorithms can suffer from premature convergence when solving complex delivery-routing problems.

This means that ants may repeatedly select similar routes before discovering the best possible route. As a result, the algorithm can get stuck with a suboptimal solution.

The research addresses this problem by proposing two improvements:
1. Dynamic Ant Population: Adjust the number of ants according to the complexity of the search.
2. Pheromone Boosting: Strengthen pheromone updates using multiple high-quality solutions to improve exploration and prevent premature convergence.
